    "start_byte": 22726,
    "text": "theorem isPureState_rootState : MathlibAnnex.CStarAlgebra.IsPureState Limit rootState"
  },
  "content": {
    "assumptions": "The embeddings come from $a\\mapsto a\\otimes I_2$. The index $0$ is the distinguished first coordinate in each stage. The coordinate functionals are compatible and bounded by the matrix norm, so they extend to the specified functional $\\omega$ on the completion. Positivity and $\\omega(1)=1$ are established before the purity argument. Convex combinations use real coefficients.",
    "conclusion": "If $\\varphi$ and $\\psi$ are states on $A$, $0<t<1$, and $\\omega=t\\varphi+(1-t)\\psi$, then $\\varphi=\\psi=\\omega$. Thus completion has not introduced a nontrivial convex decomposition of this state.",
    "content_completeness": "CARD_CONTENT_COMPLETE",
    "definition_explanation": null,
    "display_title": "Purity of the completed root state",
    "language_tag": "en",
    "lean_realization_notes": "The purity asserted here is extremality in the state space. The proof uses the pure finite-stage restrictions and density; it makes no assertion that all states on $A$ are pure.",
    "natural_language_statement": "Let $A$ be the completed CAR algebra with stage embeddings $\\iota_n:M_{2^n}(\\mathbb C)\\to A$. Let $\\omega:A\\to\\mathbb C$ be the continuous linear functional characterized by $\\omega(\\iota_n(a))=a_{00}$ for every stage matrix $a$. Then $\\omega$ is a pure state: it is an extreme point of the convex set of continuous positive unital complex-linear functionals on $A$.",
    "one_sentence_role": "Passes extremality of the root vector states from every finite matrix stage to the completed CAR algebra.",
    "proof_steps": [
      {
        "step_id": "s1",
        "text": "Write $\\omega=t\\varphi+(1-t)\\psi$ with states $\\varphi,\\psi$ and $0<t<1$."
      },
      {
        "step_id": "s2",
        "text": "For each $n$, compose with $\\iota_n$ to obtain a convex decomposition of $a\\mapsto a_{00}$ into states on $M_{2^n}(\\mathbb C)$."
      },
      {
        "step_id": "s3",
        "text": "Finite-stage purity forces $\\varphi\\circ \\iota_n=\\psi\\circ \\iota_n=(a\\mapsto a_{00})$."
      },
      {
        "step_id": "s4",
        "text": "Continuity and density imply $\\varphi=\\psi=\\omega$. The source uses the equivalent one-sided extreme-point criterion, establishing the first equality, which suffices."
      }
    ],
    "proof_summary": "Restrict a proposed convex decomposition of $\\omega$ to each finite matrix stage. The restriction of a state is again a state, because $\\iota_n$ is unital and preserves positivity. The root coordinate state $a\\mapsto a_{00}$ is pure on each matrix algebra, so both restricted states equal it. The two continuous functionals therefore agree with $\\omega$ on the dense union of stages, and hence on all of $A$."
  },
